course: dictionary
lesson: 1798
title: Closely: carefully, near, or strongly linked
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Closely has three main meanings, and the words around it tell you which one. «Look closely and you find surprises» means look carefully, with attention. «A dog follows closely behind» means very near. «Closely related» means linked in a strong way, like lions and tigers.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. In «The Rat ties it up with his handkerchief and looks closely», carefully fits, and the sentence still makes sense. The clues around closely are your best guide to which meaning to pick.
explain: Closely often comes with other words, like look closely, watch closely, listen closely and work closely with. Learn these as groups, because the phrase carries the meaning together.
fact: Closely is an adverb, so it tells you how something is done.
fact: Its other forms are more closely and most closely.
fact: «Closely» means carefully and with attention, as in «look closely».
fact: «Closely» means near in space or time, as in «a dog follows closely behind».
fact: «Closely related» means linked in a strong way, like lions and tigers.
exercise: «Look closely and you find surprises: shark skin made of tiny teeth.» What does closely mean here? | Far away from the sea | Loudly | *Carefully and with attention | Quickly and without thinking
exercise: «Lions and tigers are closely related.» What does closely mean here? | Painted in bright colours | Carefully, with a magnifying glass | Far apart in the jungle | *Linked in a strong way
exercise: «The Rat ties it up with his handkerchief and looks closely.» Which word tells you how he looks? | ties | clean | *closely | handkerchief
test: «A semicolon can join two full sentences that are closely linked: "It was raining; we stayed in."» What does closely linked mean? | *Strongly connected | Lost in the rain | Written in red | Far apart on the page
test: Which meaning of closely fits «Listen closely to the instructions»? | Rudely and fast | *With careful attention | Quietly, from far away | Near in time, just before lunch
exam: Ben says closely always means the same thing. What is the answer? | Yes, it only means carefully | Yes, it only means near | No, it means happy | *No, it has three main meanings, and the context shows which one
